{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "meta": {
    "id": "act_triad-where-they-pull",
    "slug": "triad-where-they-pull",
    "title": "Drill: Where They Pull",
    "summary": "B diminished and G with a raised fifth, both on strings 1-2-3, and the semitone steps that carry each of them into C."
  },
  "activity": {
    "kind": "note-play",
    "modes": ["easy", "hard"],
    "board": { "fretFrom": 0, "fretTo": 5 },
    "rounds": [
      {
        "kind": "targets",
        "id": "r_triad-where-they-pull.b-diminished",
        "prompt": [
          { "text": "B diminished, root position: " },
          { "text": "x x x 4 3 1", "marks": ["code"] },
          { "text": " — " },
          { "text": "B", "marks": ["code"] },
          { "text": ", " },
          { "text": "D", "marks": ["code"] },
          { "text": ", " },
          { "text": "F", "marks": ["code"] },
          {
            "text": ". The one diminished triad whose three notes are all in the C major scale. Play the notes one at a time and listen to how little it wants to stay there."
          }
        ],
        "targets": [
          { "string": 3, "fret": 4 },
          { "string": 2, "fret": 3 },
          { "string": 1, "fret": 1 }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "targets",
        "id": "r_triad-where-they-pull.g-augmented",
        "prompt": [
          { "text": "G augmented, first inversion: " },
          { "text": "x x x 4 4 3", "marks": ["code"] },
          { "text": " — " },
          { "text": "B", "marks": ["code"] },
          { "text": ", " },
          { "text": "D#", "marks": ["code"] },
          { "text": ", " },
          { "text": "G", "marks": ["code"] },
          {
            "text": ". A G chord with its fifth pushed up a fret. Same bass note as the last round, and it leans just as hard."
          }
        ],
        "targets": [
          { "string": 3, "fret": 4 },
          { "string": 2, "fret": 4 },
          { "string": 1, "fret": 3 }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "targets",
        "id": "r_triad-where-they-pull.home",
        "prompt": [
          { "text": "Where both of them go: C major, root position, " },
          { "text": "x x x 5 5 3", "marks": ["code"] },
          { "text": " — " },
          { "text": "C", "marks": ["code"] },
          { "text": ", " },
          { "text": "E", "marks": ["code"] },
          { "text": ", " },
          { "text": "G", "marks": ["code"] },
          {
            "text": ". Play the previous two rounds again first, then land on this one, so you hear what the tension was for."
          }
        ],
        "targets": [
          { "string": 3, "fret": 5 },
          { "string": 2, "fret": 5 },
          { "string": 1, "fret": 3 }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "targets",
        "id": "r_triad-where-they-pull.the-two-that-lean",
        "prompt": [
          {
            "text": "The two voices that move going from G augmented into C, each followed by where it lands: "
          },
          { "text": "3·4", "marks": ["code"] },
          { "text": ", " },
          { "text": "3·5", "marks": ["code"] },
          { "text": ", " },
          { "text": "2·4", "marks": ["code"] },
          { "text": ", " },
          { "text": "2·5", "marks": ["code"] },
          {
            "text": ". Two semitones, in this order. The third voice never moves at all, which is why the change costs so little."
          }
        ],
        "targets": [
          { "string": 3, "fret": 4 },
          { "string": 3, "fret": 5 },
          { "string": 2, "fret": 4 },
          { "string": 2, "fret": 5 }
        ],
        "ordered": true
      }
    ]
  }
}
